bp3 config - view the machine-local bp3 config store (<git-common-dir>/bp3/, never committed):
bp3 config [--source] [--format json|table]   thresholds plus contexts folded from runs/<run_id>.json
config.json holds machine settings only (thresholds: setup_slow_s, depth_cap); contexts are views, never stored there. First call on a fresh repo creates the store with defaults (zero setup), and every view rebuilds the derived by-session index from runs/, so deleting by-session/ loses nothing. --source names the writing verb and timestamp per context. Outside a git repo there is no store and the call refuses E_NOT_FOUND.
